  #
  # This looks up the sender address in the DNS
  # and will fail if nothing is registered for the PTR
  # which is common with spammers.
  #
  # Originally this used defer_never, however this setting
  # produces a complete ban if there are problems with the DNS
  # lookup, which happens, albeit rarely. This now uses defer_strict
  # which doesn't produce a fail if the DNS fails.
  #
  #
  # Wise to only use this if running a local caching DNS server

  deny !condition = ${lookup dnsdb{defer_strict,ptr=$sender_host_address}{yes}}
       message = No reverse DNS record found
